    ],
    "method": "Stratified sample: one fixed hour (12:00-12:59 UTC) per sampled day, every transaction in that hour decoded (not a random sample of the day). Method shares describe that hour only and can be biased by time-of-day patterns and by single large callers. Distinct callers per sampled hour are LOWER BOUNDS for distinct callers per day and must not be scaled up or compared with all-day or all-time counts. Transactions are classified by the first receipt addressed to v1.signer whose predecessor is not v1.signer itself (callbacks are ignored); wrapper methods such as sign_transfer and sign_btc_transaction appear under tx_entry_method and resolve to sign at the v1.signer level. Methods starting with respond_ (respond_ckd, respond_verify_foreign_tx) are node-side responses counted in primary_respond_other. The domain label legacy_key_version_N marks sign requests in the older argument format that carries key_version and no domain_id; their signature scheme is not decoded here.",
